# .gitignore for a bioinformatics project — copy to the project root as `.gitignore`.
#
# Principle (Noble 2009, Wilson 2017): version-control ONLY hand-edited files.
# Generated outputs live in stage subdirectories of each results/ experiment dir and
# are regenerable by `runall`, so they are ignored. Hand-written files directly in an
# experiment dir (driver, README, Snakefile, config.yaml, main.nf, one-off scripts)
# and the lab notebook stay tracked.
#
# NOTE: git only treats `#` as a comment at the START of a line. Never put a comment
# on the same line as a pattern — it becomes part of the pattern and silently breaks.

# --- Raw data: large, immutable, deposited to a repository; never in git ---------
data/raw/
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.fasta.gz
*.bam
*.bai
*.sam
*.cram

# --- Environments / caches -------------------------------------------------------
.pixi/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- results/: ignore generated outputs, keep hand-written files ---------------
# Layout: results/<date>_<name>/<stage>/. The files directly inside an experiment
# dir are hand-written (driver, README, workflow and config files, one-off scripts)
# and stay tracked. Everything inside a stage subdirectory is generated.
#
# Ignore every stage subdirectory of every experiment dir ...
results/*/*/
# ... the provenance file that runall regenerates ...
results/*/provenance.txt
# ... and the shared taxonomy output (fixed path, written by the taxonomy stage).
results/taxonomy/*

# --- Working notes stay local; tasks/METHODS.md is analysis provenance ---------
tasks/*
!tasks/METHODS.md

# --- Compiled third-party tools in bin/ (track only your own wrappers) -----------
bin/checkm
bin/*.bin
